<article class="env-definition" id="07LS">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/07LS">Definition <span data-tag="07LS">13.37.1</span>.</a> Let $\mathcal{D}$ be an additive category with arbitrary direct sums. A <em>compact object</em> of $\mathcal{D}$ is an object $K$ such that the map </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  \bigoplus \nolimits _{i \in I} \mathop{\mathrm{Hom}}\nolimits _{\mathcal{D}}(K, E_ i) \longrightarrow \mathop{\mathrm{Hom}}\nolimits _{\mathcal{D}}(K, \bigoplus \nolimits _{i \in I} E_ i)  \]
</div>
  <p> is bijective for any set $I$ and objects $E_ i \in \mathop{\mathrm{Ob}}\nolimits (\mathcal{D})$ parametrized by $i \in I$. </p>
</article>